    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103889" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῐάρᾱ</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱρ], ἡ</span>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῐάρας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῐήρης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span> (as in <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			8.120
		</span></i>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tiara</i>, the Persian head-dress, esp. on solemn occasions,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.132
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.12
			</span></i> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῖλος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				7.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.120
			</span></i>; worn by the great king, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				661
			</span></i> (lyr.); whose tiara was upright, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.5.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.3.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				22J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pisc.</u>
				35
			</span></i>.</div>
